### arxiv_2204.00770

In this work, we propose a simple yet effective adaptation (finetuning) strategy named "[wav2vec2](SPEECH_TECH:TEC006) adapter" to incorporate [wav2vec2](SPEECH_TECH:TEC006) with [speaker adaptation](SPEECH_TECH:TEC015). Here, we attempt to finetune the [wav2vec2](SPEECH_TECH:TEC006) by feeding speaker information as auxiliary features during fine-tuning to efficiently finetune the [wav2vec2](SPEECH_TECH:TEC006) model parameters. An adapter network containing a bottleneck layer is instilled into the context encoder network of [wav2vec2](SPEECH_TECH:TEC006) model to integrate the auxiliary features and [wav2vec2](SPEECH_TECH:TEC006) outputs. The adapter module is based on the recent works [16, 17] on machine translation to fine-tune pre-trained transformer models. The primary contributions of this work are as follows:

