### pubmed_40409971

Objectives A consensus study to establish a Core Outcome Set for [dysarthria](DISORDER:DIS001) after [stroke](DISORDER:DIS014) identified four key outcome domains that should be measured in research and clinical practice: (1) [intelligibility](SPEECH_FEATURE:SPF001) of speech, (2) ability to participate in conversations, (3) living well with [dysarthria](DISORDER:DIS001) and (4) communication partners skills and knowledge (where relevant). This review aimed to systematically identify corresponding measurement instruments and to examine their clinical utility and psychometric properties. Design Systematic review conducted in alignment with the Preferred Reporting Items for Systematic Reviews and Meta-­Analyses guidelines.

